; tests/print-value-kinds-band.fk — the byte-equality gate for `print`, the VALUE printer.
;
; Prelude-free on purpose: every form below is a primitive, so all four arms run this
; band directly and validate.sh compares their WHOLE captured output with `==`. That
; comparison IS the assertion — the verdict attests the fixture, the printed stream
; attests the printer. A band that only returned a number could not gate a printer;
; the point of this one is the lines it writes.
;
; WHY IT EXISTS. Until 2026-07-31 fkwu carried print_str (115, the bytes of a string)
; but no `print`, so under `fkwu --src` every (print ..) matched no op and lowered to
; nothing (axiom-5) — LOUD as a diagnostic, NUMB in the stream: a printer function
; emitted nothing, and a carrier reading that stream read an empty answer as an empty
; result. MEASURED before the change, driving form-stdlib/mla-demo.fk's mld-emit-all:
; bin-go wrote 277 lines, fkwu wrote 1. After it, the two streams are byte-identical.
;
; WHAT THESE LINES PIN — the places the arms could disagree and don't:
;   - a bare string, and a str_concat string (the two ways a string value is born)
;   - an int, and a negative int
;   - a non-integral float, and an INTEGRAL float: 3.0 prints "3", never "3.0"
;   - 999999.0 — the last value before Go's shortest-'g' exponent cliff
;   - a repeating fraction — every digit of the shortest round-tripping decimal
;   - two operands, and three MIXED operands: variadic, one space BETWEEN, one newline
;     after (not a newline per operand)
;   - (print) with no operands at all — the bare newline, not silence
;
; WHAT THIS BAND DELIBERATELY DOES NOT PRINT, and why it would be dishonest to.
; Three kinds were measured on all four arms on 2026-07-31 and the SIBLINGS diverge
; from each other — this band predates any decision about which is canon, so pinning
; one here would freeze one arm's accident as law:
;
;     source        go       rust                       ts        (real JS)
;     1000000.0     1e+06    1000000                    1000000   1000000
;     0.00001       1e-05    0.00001                    0.00001   0.00001
;     1e21          1e+21    1000000000000000000000     1e+21     1e+21
;     0.0000001     1e-07    0.0000001                  1e-7      1e-7
;     (list 1 2)    [1, 2]   [1, 2]                     [1 2]     —
;
; Two separate seams. FLOATS: go's core.FormatFloatJS is named for, and documented as,
; "JS String(number) semantics", but calls strconv.FormatFloat(f,'g',-1,64) — a rule
; with different exponent thresholds and zero-padded exponents. TS (actual JS) is the
; arm that matches the stated intent; go is the outlier against its own contract.
; LISTS: go and rust join elements ", " and ts joins " ". fkwu was made to match GO
; byte-for-byte here, because that is what the work asked for and go is what the
; fourth arm is compared against — but "fkwu agrees with go" is not "the kernels
; agree", and this table is the witness that they do not.
;
; Also NOT pinned: print's RETURN value. go answers VNull, fkwu answers 0, and
; `(eq (print "x") 0)` PANICS on bin-go ("as_int: null") while fkwu answers 1. That
; belongs to the no-value contract eq/nothing/null share across all four arms, not to
; the printer.

(do
    (print "a string")
    (print (str_concat "cat" "dog"))
    (print 42)
    (print -7)
    (print 3.5)
    (print 3.0)
    (print 999999.0)
    (print (div 1.0 3.0))
    (print "two" "words")
    (print 1 2.5 "three")
    (print)

    ;; The verdict attests the FIXTURE — that each value handed to print above was
    ;; built as intended, so a broken fixture cannot quietly print a green stream.
    ;; Power-of-two weights: every claim keeps its own bit, so the verdict NAMES which
    ;; claim fell instead of folding into a sum two failures could forge between them.
    (let ok-concat   (if (str_eq (str_concat "cat" "dog") "catdog") 1 0))
    (let ok-integral (if (eq 3.0 3) 2 0))
    (let ok-cliff    (if (lt 999999.0 1000000.0) 4 0))
    (let ok-third    (if (lt (div 1.0 3.0) 3.5) 8 0))
    (let ok-neg      (if (lt -7 42) 16 0))
    (let ok-str      (if (str_eq "a string" "a string") 32 0))

    ;; Band verdict: 63 when every fixture claim crosses.
    (add ok-concat (add ok-integral (add ok-cliff (add ok-third (add ok-neg ok-str))))))
